cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use HumanTracker, please cite it as below."
title: "HumanTracker: Towards Comprehensive and Human-Aligned Motion Tracking Benchmark"
abstract: >-
  HumanTracker is a humanoid motion tracking benchmark contributing approximately 153
  hours of newly captured optical motion from 24 professional performers across four
  motion families, together with HumanScore, a preference-aligned metric trained on
  12K human-labeled preference pairs spanning 24K synchronized tracker trajectories via
  a trajectory reward model. Accepted to ECCV 2026.
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://dairuliu.github.io/humantracker/"
